+---
+id: task-004-bulk-import-helper-importtasks
+type: task
+title: "Bulk import helper importTasks"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Bulk import helper importTasks
+
+Teams are moving to Tidy Tasks from their spreadsheets. They need a public helper that adds many tasks from
+text in one go: one task per line.
+
+## What to build
+
+- `importTasks(list, text)`, exported from `src/index.ts`. `list` is a `TaskList`; `text` is the pasted text.
+- Each line holds one task as `title;priority;tags`:
+  - the title, trimmed;
+  - the priority, which may be left empty for a normal one; otherwise it is checked as `add` checks it;
+  - the tags, separated by spaces; they may be left empty.
+- A line must have exactly three `;`-separated fields. Any other count is rejected, with a reason that says
+  the expected form is `title;priority;tags`.
+- Blank lines are skipped. Line numbers count from 1, blank lines included.
+- Every valid line is added to the list through `list.add`, so the same checks apply: an empty or over-long
+  title, an unknown priority, an empty tag, or a title already in the list is rejected.
+- Each line is handled on its own: a rejected line does not stop the others from being added.
+- The helper returns `{ imported, rejected }`: `imported` is how many tasks were added; `rejected` lists every
+  line that could not be added as `{ line, reason }`, where `reason` is the message the list gave, or the
+  format message above.
+- The helper does not throw (directive r4) and does not read the clock (directive r3): the list stamps the
+  tasks.
+- Exported functions and types carry TSDoc (directive r2). No new dependency (directive r1).
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- A line `Renew the insurance;high;admin money` adds a high-priority task tagged `admin` and `money`.
+- A line with an empty priority, `Buy milk;;home`, adds a normal-priority task.
+- A line with no tags, `Buy milk;;`, adds a task with no tags.
+- Blank lines and lines of only spaces are skipped, and are not counted as rejected.
+- A line with an unknown priority, an empty or space-only title, an over-long title, or an empty tag is
+  rejected with the reason from `add`, and nothing is added for it.
+- A line with the wrong number of fields is rejected, with a reason naming the `title;priority;tags` form.
+- A title already in the list, or repeated in the text, is rejected as a duplicate; the first one is kept.
+- The `line` of each rejection is the line's number in the text, counting from 1.
+- `importTasks` on an empty text returns `{ imported: 0, rejected: [] }`.
